WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.498
Local language-model performance is a user experience, not one benchmark number.

00:00:05.498 --> 00:00:10.996
Time to first token measures the delay before useful output begins.

00:00:10.996 --> 00:00:16.055
That delay includes model loading, queueing, tokenization, and prompt processing.

00:00:16.055 --> 00:00:23.752
Generation speed, commonly reported as tokens per second, describes how quickly output continues after generation starts.

00:00:23.752 --> 00:00:32.329
A system can generate quickly yet feel slow if it spends a long time ingesting a large prompt.

00:00:32.329 --> 00:00:40.906
Throughput is the amount of useful work completed over time, especially when several requests or documents are processed.

00:00:40.906 --> 00:00:45.525
Latency is the delay experienced by an individual request.

00:00:45.525 --> 00:00:51.463
Batching and concurrency may improve throughput while making one user wait longer.

00:00:51.463 --> 00:00:55.201
Stability also belongs in the performance definition.

00:00:55.201 --> 00:01:04.218
A fast configuration that runs out of memory, overheats, crashes, or produces unacceptable output is not an optimized system.

00:01:04.218 --> 00:01:15.434
Synthetic benchmarks are useful for controlled comparison, but real workflows include context length, retrieval results, code files, document parsing, network interfaces, and repeated sessions.

00:01:15.434 --> 00:01:22.252
Measure the task that matters: interactive chat, coding completion, summarization, embeddings, or batch extraction.

00:01:22.252 --> 00:01:30.389
Record model, quantization, runtime, prompt, context setting, hardware state, and temperature so a result can be reproduced.

00:01:30.389 --> 00:01:33.248
Optimization starts with a baseline.

00:01:33.248 --> 00:01:40.506
Run a repeatable workload, observe each stage, and identify the constrained resource before changing anything.

00:01:40.506 --> 00:01:46.444
Then alter one variable and compare speed, memory, quality, power, and stability.

00:01:46.444 --> 00:01:53.261
Guessing encourages expensive upgrades and random settings; measurement turns tuning into an engineering process.
